Chapter: TailSelfOverApply
  cites Foreword chapter Console

Section: Body

 Polymorphic recursion at a type-variable result: `h (n - 1)` is an `a`
 instantiated as Integer -> a, so the tail self-call carries one argument
 more than `h` takes, and is a call followed by an application rather than a
 jump (COMPILER-139).

  h : Integer -> a
  h (n) = if n == 0 then fail "reached zero" else h (n - 1) 5

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    trying 1 times
      print-line-uni (show (h 3))
    falling back to
      print-line-uni "fallback"
    end
  end
